"""Regenerate port/manifest.tsv from the vendored libslic3r tree.

Walk every ``.h``, ``.hpp``, ``.cpp`` and ``.mm`` file under
``vendor/OrcaSlicer/src/libslic3r`` and write one manifest row per file, filling only the
four columns this task owns: path, subsystem, lines and the file-level include-DAG level.
The remaining eleven columns are later parts of plan step 11's work and are left empty here.

The row set always comes from the filesystem walk, never from
``src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt``. That build file is parsed only to cross-check that every
file it names also has a row, because the build file itself omits files that are produced by
other means (an orphan pass, dead code still compiled in, Apple-only sources).
"""

